2026-09-25T03:59:37.0231836Z [36;1m# Desktop-update hand-off integration tests spawn the real[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0232305Z [36;1m# windows.ps1; deselect them unless the PR touched that surface[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0232831Z [36;1m# (see the workflow_call input). ``--ignore-glob`` keeps the file[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0233295Z [36;1m# list above intact, so a renamed test file still trips the[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0233889Z [36;1m# zero-tests guard rather than silently vanishing.[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0234340Z [36;1m# (bash 3.2 on the macOS runner: an empty array under ``set -u`` is[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0234753Z [36;1m# an unbound-variable error, hence the ``${arr[@]+...}`` idiom.)[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0235087Z [36;1mEXTRA_ARGS=()[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0235295Z [36;1mif [ "false" != "true" ]; then[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0235748Z [36;1m  echo "desktop_updater lane off: skipping tests/scripts/desktop_update/test_desktop_update_windows_*.py"[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0236306Z [36;1m  EXTRA_ARGS+=(--ignore-glob='*test_desktop_update_windows_*.py')[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0236626Z [36;1mfi[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0236777Z [36;1m[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0237011Z [36;1m# ``tr -d '\r'``: on Windows the helper's redirected stdout gains[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0237412Z [36;1m# CRLF line endings; a stray \r would corrupt the path. The list[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0237812Z [36;1m# uses the native path-list separator consumed by --files.[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0238112Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0238357Z [36;1m# Any non-zero exit propagates red: real test failures, or the[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0238758Z [36;1m# runner's own zero-run guard (every file filtered to empty by[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0239168Z [36;1m# ``-m`` — "must never pass without running its OS's tests").[0m
2026-09-25T03:59:37.0239596Z [36;1mSEPARATOR="$(python -c 'import os, sys; sys.stdout.write(os.pathsep)')"[0m
